e defect and is not part of this account.\\\"]}\n]\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nprint('patched ok')\nPYEOF\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\np='draft/update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['rationale']=(\\\"Second finding on hashicorp/raft startup: with Config.RestoreCommittedLogs enabled, restoreFromCommittedLogs calls processLogs before NewRaft starts the FSM goroutine, so a committed backlog larger than the 128-slot FSM queue can never be drained and NewRaft never returns. Receipt 04fccedbacf54df3b7064fd16fa57b26 (exit 0, ten events, no parse loss) witnesses the violation: the above-buffer case emitted newraft_returned false after a bounded 15 second wait with 8402 committed entries and no snapshot, so comparison 0 is violated with witness event index 9. The control comparison came back unknown only because both backlog cases shared one result event name, which made the controller look for the other case's admission under each comparison; its event still shows newraft_returned true after 0 ms for 8002 entries. The corrected declaration splits the result event names per case and is submitted as a successor experiment so the control can complete. The configuration-loss question stays as previously recorded and is not restated here.\\\")\nd['sources']=[\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":724,\\\"end_line\\\":754,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_fsm_mutate_buffer\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":558,\\\"end_line\\\":561,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_goroutines_after_restore\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":632,\\\"end_line\\\":639,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"raft_processlogs_applybatch\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1296,\\\"end_line\\\":1320,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_restore_committed_call\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":604,\\\"end_line\\\":620,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_restore_snapshot_config\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":655,\\\"end_line\\\":681,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"log_commit_tracking_iface\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"log.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":194,\\\"end_line\\\":219,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"interface_statement\\\"}\n]\nd['knowledge']=[\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"ef5ddbf78bd4456ea51537bd60a61a80-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"fact\\\",\n  \\\"statement\\\":\\\"At startup the in-memory configuration (r.configurations.latest/committed) is produced only by restoreSnapshot (the latest snapshot's configuration) and by the NewRaft log scan over indexes greater than max(snapshotIndex, lastApplied). With Config.RestoreCommittedLogs enabled, restoreFromCommittedLogs sets lastApplied to the persisted commit index before that scan, so a committed LogConfiguration entry at an index <= the restored commit index is never processed and the node keeps the snapshot configuration, or an empty configuration when no snapshot exists.\\\",\n  \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Config.RestoreCommittedLogs=true with a LogStore implementing CommitTrackingLogStore; the persisted commit index from GetCommitIndex is at least the index of the latest committed LogConfiguration entry; no snapshot covers that entry (no snapshot at all, or snapshot.ConfigurationIndex below it).\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_restore_committed_call\\\",\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"api_restore_snapshot_config\\\",\\\"log_commit_tracking_iface\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"75c355f2a4634b5193fa97e4de987fe0\\\":[1,3,4,5],\\\"3e2dd223dd5f43409c21066a1ca43175\\\":[1,3]}},\n {\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@newraft_blocked_fact\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n  \\\"statement\\\":\\\"With Config.RestoreCommittedLogs enabled and no snapshot, NewRaft replays the committed log by pushing one fsmMutateCh message per MaxAppendEntries-sized batch before the FSM goroutine is started; when the committed backlog requires more batches than the queue's 128 slots the send blocks and NewRaft never returns, so the node never starts.\\\",\n  \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Config.RestoreCommittedLogs=true with a CommitTrackingLogStore, no snapshot covering the committed range, and a restored commit index whose replay needs more than 128 batches of MaxAppendEntries entries (default 64, about 8192 entries); observed for 8402 entries (132 batches) with a bounded 15 second wait, against 8002 entries (126 batches) returning in 0-3 ms.\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"api_fsm_mutate_buffer\\\",\\\"api_goroutines_after_restore\\\",\\\"raft_processlogs_applybatch\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"04fccedbacf54df3b7064fd16fa57b26\\\":[7,9]}}\n]\nd['experiment']={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"8c72cf483b114ffd808643c17dfa6945-question-1\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n \\\"previous_id\\\":\\\"8c72cf483b114ffd808643c17dfa6945-experiment\\\",\n \\\"revision_reason\\\":\\\"Only the comparison declaration and the per-case result event names change: each backlog size now emits its own result event (restart_backlog_below / restart_backlog_above) so each comparison sees exactly one result event and can complete. Inputs, sizes, bounded wait and assertions are unchanged.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"api_fsm_mutate_buffer\\\",\\\"api_goroutines_after_restore\\\",\\\"raft_processlogs_applybatch\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Boot one node with RestoreCommittedLogs on and a CommitTrackingLogStore, commit 8000 and then (separately) 8400 entries without any snapshot, restart from the same stores, and report whether NewRaft returns within a bounded 15 second wait.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"MaxAppendEntries keeps its default of 64, so 8002 committed entries need 126 batches while 8402 need 132.\\\",\\\"No snapshot is taken, so restoreFromCommittedLogs replays the whole committed log.\\\",\\\"The two sizes bracket the FSM queue capacity without changing any production logic.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"Whole-package or repository test suites.\\\",\\\"Any judgment about how long a large but sub-capacity replay may legitimately take.\\\",\\\"The configuration-loss finding, recorded under the parent question.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"entries_below\\\":8000,\\\"entries_above\\\":8400,\\\"bounded_wait_seconds\\\":15}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"The harness uses the package's own test facilities (inmemConfig, MakeClusterOpts with CommitTrackingLogs, MakeClusterCustom), commits the entries through Apply, shuts the node down, then calls NewRaft on a separate goroutine so the test can report a bounded wait. Each case emits a startup_before_restart event and then its own result event (restart_backlog_below or restart_backlog_above) carrying newraft_returned, restart_wait_ms and the same operands; no production logic is modified.\\\",\n \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"The library owns startup: NewRaft must either return or fail, and must not depend on a component it starts only after returning.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"below_buffer\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"startup_before_restart\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"below_buffer\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"above_buffer\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"startup_before_restart\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"above_buffer\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0}]}],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"restart_backlog_above\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"above_buffer\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\